**Validate seed `phase` in `makeQuarantineLedger`.**

`src/adapters/store/quarantine.ts:110` passes `record.phase` to `upsert` without a runtime check. The type is the single literal `'verifier-failed'`. Library consumers that restore state from JSON can pass any string at runtime. The ledger then stores and returns that tag.

The module header says the tag stops a future entry path from masquerading as a verifier failure. Reject unknown phases in seeds, or document that seeds are trusted.

<details>
<summary>Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
   for (const record of initial ?? []) {
+    if (record.phase !== QUARANTINE_PHASE) {
+      throw new RangeError(`quarantine ledger: unknown phase '${String(record.phase)}' for '${record.playbookId}'`);
+    }
     upsert(record.playbookId, record.reason, record.phase);
   }
```
</details>

**`absorb()` caches an unterminated tail before it rejects it, and reads the file twice.**

Line 134 reads the file. Lines 135-144 add every valid-looking record to `known`, including a final 32-hex record that has no newline. Line 146 then calls `hasUnterminatedTail`, which reads the file a second time. This throws after the tail is already in `known`.

- This contradicts the contract at Lines 98-99. That contract says an unterminated record is "never accepted as committed history". The throw makes this inconsistent: the nonce is absent from the committed ledger but stays in the in-process cache.
- If an operator repairs the ledger by removing the unterminated tail, a long-lived instance still returns `'spent'` for that nonce. This is the safe direction, but memory and file no longer agree.
- `spent()` and `isSpent()` call `absorb()` without `appendLock`. A concurrent appender can change the file between the two reads. The result is a spurious malformed-record or unterminated-tail throw. `consumeLocked` is not affected, because it holds the lock.

Read the file once. Check the tail on that same string before you populate `known`. Then `hasUnterminatedTail` (Lines 351-356) has no callers and can be removed.

<details>
<summary>Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
     if (!existsSync(path)) return;
-    const lines = readFileSync(path, 'utf8').split('\n');
+    const contents = readFileSync(path, 'utf8');
+    // Validate the tail before ANY record enters `known`.
+    if (contents !== '' && !contents.endsWith('\n')) {
+      throw new Error(
+        `approval ledger: '${path}' ends with an unterminated record — the ledger is fail-closed until an operator inspects and repairs it`,
+      );
+    }
+    const lines = contents.split('\n');
     lines.forEach((line, index) => {
       ...
       known.add(record);
     });
-    // Validate before ANY spent lookup, including read-only inspection.
-    if (hasUnterminatedTail(path)) {
-      throw new Error(
-        `approval ledger: '${path}' ends with an unterminated record — the ledger is fail-closed until an operator inspects and repairs it`,
-      );
-    }
   };
```
</details>
